CONF68K known divergencesTest IDs listed here are disagreements with DOCS/claims.md that havealready been investigated and characterised. The runner reports them asKNOWN rather than as new findings, so that a familiar defect does notdrown out a fresh one. A line is "<test-id> <one-line explanation>".An empty list is the intended steady state: it means every claim inclaims.md holds on every system we can currently reach. It is emptyagain as of 2026-07-31. The record-locking tests found five divergences ontheir first run against an RBF image, all of them os9exec's rather thanOS-9's, and all five have since been fixed -- see git log for t19, t23,t25, t27 and t29.Those findings were all RBF-image ones. On a host-native directory thelocking tests report SKIP and prove nothing, which is why DOCS/expected andDOCS/expected-rbf remain separate files.